","\u002Finternals\u002Fwolf","7.internals\u002F6.wolf",{"id":213,"title":101,"body":214,"description":635,"extension":636,"links":637,"meta":638,"navigation":639,"path":102,"seo":640,"stem":103,"__hash__":641},"docs_en\u002F4.alerts\u002F3.channels.md",{"type":215,"value":216,"toc":625},"minimark",[217,229,235,240,389,392,396,440,444,462,466,477,481,498,502,520,532,556,565,573,612],[218,219,220,221,224,225,228],"p",{},"Each row of a rule's ",[222,223,101],"strong",{}," (or ",[222,226,227],{},"Escalation Channels",") table is one destination. Secrets\n(tokens, keys, webhook URLs) are Password fields: stored encrypted, never logged, and scrubbed from\nevery recorded error.",[218,230,231,234],{},[222,232,233],{},"Send test notification"," on the rule form sends a TEST to every enabled row and shows what each\none answered.",[236,237,239],"h2",{"id":238},"types","Types",[241,242,243,259],"table",{},[244,245,246],"thead",{},[247,248,249,253,256],"tr",{},[250,251,252],"th",{},"Type",[250,254,255],{},"Sends",[250,257,258],{},"Settings",[260,261,262,274,295,306,317,327,341,352,363,374],"tbody",{},[247,263,264,268,271],{},[265,266,267],"td",{},"Email",[265,269,270],{},"one email per recipient, with signed Acknowledge \u002F Resolve links",[265,272,273],{},"Recipients",[247,275,276,279,292],{},[265,277,278],{},"Webhook",[265,280,281,282,286,287,291],{},"generic JSON ",[283,284,285],"code",{},"{text, incident}"," (",[288,289,290],"a",{"href":159},"protocol",")",[265,293,294],{},"Webhook URL",[247,296,297,300,303],{},[265,298,299],{},"Raven",[265,301,302],{},"a message in a Raven channel",[265,304,305],{},"Raven Channel",[247,307,308,311,314],{},[265,309,310],{},"Slack",[265,312,313],{},"Block Kit message with a severity colour bar and Open \u002F Acknowledge \u002F Resolve buttons",[265,315,316],{},"Incoming Webhook URL*",[247,318,319,322,325],{},[265,320,321],{},"Mattermost",[265,323,324],{},"message attachment with colour, fields and Acknowledge \u002F Resolve links",[265,326,316],{},[247,328,329,332,338],{},[265,330,331],{},"Matrix",[265,333,334,337],{},[283,335,336],{},"m.room.message"," with an HTML body",[265,339,340],{},"Homeserver URL, Room ID, Access Token*",[247,342,343,346,349],{},[265,344,345],{},"ntfy",[265,347,348],{},"push with title, priority, tags, click and action buttons",[265,350,351],{},"Server URL (default ntfy.sh), Topic, Access Token* (optional)",[247,353,354,357,360],{},[265,355,356],{},"Gotify",[265,358,359],{},"push with priority mapped from severity and a click URL",[265,361,362],{},"Server URL, Application Token*",[247,364,365,368,371],{},[265,366,367],{},"SMS",[265,369,370],{},"short text (one or two SMS) through any HTTP gateway",[265,372,373],{},"Phone Numbers, Gateway URL template, Method, Body, Auth Header, Secret*, Max Length",[247,375,376,379,386],{},[265,377,378],{},"PagerDuty",[265,380,381,382,385],{},"Events API v2: trigger, acknowledge, resolve; ",[283,383,384],{},"dedup_key"," = incident name",[265,387,388],{},"Routing Key*, Events API URL",[218,390,391],{},"* Password field: stored encrypted, shown as asterisks.",[236,393,395],{"id":394},"who-hears-what","Who hears what",[397,398,399,409,423,429,432],"ul",{},[400,401,402,403,405,406,408],"li",{},"Opened and reopened incidents go to the ",[222,404,101],{},"; escalations to the ",[222,407,227],{},".",[400,410,411,412,414,415,418,419,422],{},"When someone acknowledges or resolves an incident (Desk or a signed link), ",[222,413,378],{}," channels\nalways get the matching ",[283,416,417],{},"acknowledge"," \u002F ",[283,420,421],{},"resolve"," event, so the alert closes on call too.",[400,424,425,426,408],{},"The other channels hear a resolution only when the rule has ",[222,427,428],{},"Notify On Resolve",[400,430,431],{},"A test from the rule form triggers then resolves on PagerDuty, so it never leaves an alert open.",[400,433,434,435,439],{},"During a ",[288,436,438],{"href":437},"\u002Falerts\u002Frules#maintenance-windows","maintenance window",", notifications wait until it ends.",[236,441,443],{"id":442},"signed-action-links","Signed action links",[218,445,446,447,418,450,453,454,457,458,461],{},"Alerts for unresolved incidents carry signed ",[222,448,449],{},"Acknowledge",[222,451,452],{},"Resolve"," links, valid 24 h\n(",[222,455,456],{},"Wolf Settings → Action Link Hours","). Opening a link shows a confirmation page; only its button\nacts, so mail scanners cannot acknowledge for you. Security incidents also carry a link per\n",[288,459,460],{"href":81},"response action"," Wolf proposes; those ask for a Wolf Manager's login.",[236,463,465],{"id":464},"delivery-status","Delivery status",[218,467,468,469,472,473,476],{},"Every attempt is recorded as a ",[222,470,471],{},"Wolf Delivery",": channel, target without secrets, kind, PagerDuty\naction, ok or error, HTTP status. The incident lists them under ",[222,474,475],{},"Deliveries",". Deliveries follow\nthe event retention.",[236,478,480],{"id":479},"upgrading-from-01","Upgrading from 0.1",[218,482,483,484,487,488,492,493,497],{},"Digests were removed in 0.2: every channel sends each alert at once. A channel that used hourly\ndigests in 0.1 now gets every alert as it happens. Digests still pending at the upgrade are\ndropped, not sent: the upgrade prints how many and records the count in an ",[222,485,486],{},"Error Log"," titled\n",[489,490,491],"em",{},"Dodock Wolf 0.2: pending digests dropped",". Release ",[288,494,496],{"href":495},"\u002Fgetting-started#staying-on-v010","v0.1.0","\nkeeps digests.",[236,499,501],{"id":500},"setup-per-type","Setup per type",[503,504,505],"collapsible",{"name":310},[218,506,507,508,511,512,515,516,519],{},"Create an app → ",[222,509,510],{},"Incoming Webhooks"," → ",[222,513,514],{},"Add New Webhook to Workspace",", and paste the\n",[283,517,518],{},"https:\u002F\u002Fhooks.slack.com\u002Fservices\u002F…"," URL. Buttons open the incident or the signed action page, so no\nSlack interactivity endpoint is needed. Slack may show a warning icon on link buttons of apps\nwithout one.",[503,521,522],{"name":321},[218,523,524,527,528,531],{},[222,525,526],{},"Integrations → Incoming Webhooks → Add",", and paste the ",[283,529,530],{},"https:\u002F\u002F…\u002Fhooks\u002F…"," URL.",[503,533,534],{"name":331},[218,535,536,537,540,541,544,545,548,549,552,553,408],{},"Create a bot account, invite it to the room and join. Get its access token (Element: ",[222,538,539],{},"Settings →\nHelp & About → Access Token",", or ",[283,542,543],{},"POST \u002F_matrix\u002Fclient\u002Fv3\u002Flogin","). The Room ID is the internal\n",[283,546,547],{},"!…:server"," one (",[222,550,551],{},"Room settings → Advanced","), not an alias. Messages are sent with\n",[283,554,555],{},"PUT \u002F_matrix\u002Fclient\u002Fv3\u002Frooms\u002F{room}\u002Fsend\u002F…",[503,557,558],{"name":345},[218,559,560,561,564],{},"Any topic on ntfy.sh or your own server. On a public server, pick an unguessable topic, or protect it\nand paste an access token (",[283,562,563],{},"tk_…","). Priority: critical 5, warning 4, info 3, resolved 2; escalations\none step higher.",[503,566,567],{"name":356},[218,568,569,572],{},[222,570,571],{},"Apps → Create application",", and paste its token. Priority: critical 8, warning 5, info 3,\nresolved 2; escalations two steps higher.",[503,574,575,598,601],{"name":367},[218,576,577,578,581,582,585,586,589,590,593,594,597],{},"Provider agnostic. The Gateway URL and the optional Body Template take ",[283,579,580],{},"{to}",", ",[283,583,584],{},"{text}"," and\n",[283,587,588],{},"{secret}"," placeholders: URL-encoded in the URL and form bodies, JSON-escaped in JSON bodies. The Auth\nHeader is a header line such as ",[283,591,592],{},"Authorization: Bearer {secret}",". Put API keys in ",[222,595,596],{},"Secret",", never\nin the URL. One request per phone number.",[218,599,600],{},"The text (kind, severity, title, scope, and the incident URL when it fits) is folded to the GSM-7\nalphabet and cut on a word boundary to 160 characters (one SMS) or 306 (two). Text that needs\nUnicode fits 70 \u002F 134.",[602,603,610],"pre",{"className":604,"code":606,"filename":607,"language":608,"meta":609},[605],"language-text","Gateway URL:   https:\u002F\u002Fsms.example.com\u002Fapi\u002Fsend\nMethod \u002F Body: POST, json, {\"to\": \"{to}\", \"message\": \"{text}\"}\nAuth Header:   Authorization: Bearer {secret}\n","A gateway that takes JSON","text","",[283,611,606],{"__ignoreMap":609},[503,613,614],{"name":378},[218,615,616,617,620,621,624],{},"Add an ",[222,618,619],{},"Events API v2"," integration to a service and paste its integration key as the Routing Key.\nChange the Events API URL for the EU region (",[283,622,623],{},"https:\u002F\u002Fevents.eu.pagerduty.com\u002Fv2\u002Fenqueue","), or for an\nEvents-v2 compatible receiver: Grafana OnCall, Opsgenie and others accept the same body.",{"title":609,"searchDepth":626,"depth":627,"links":628},1,2,[629,630,631,632,633,634],{"id":238,"depth":627,"text":239},{"id":394,"depth":627,"text":395},{"id":442,"depth":627,"text":443},{"id":464,"depth":627,"text":465},{"id":479,"depth":627,"text":480},{"id":500,"depth":627,"text":501},"Send alerts to email, chat, push, SMS or PagerDuty, and set up each destination.","md",null,{},{"icon":104},{"title":101,"description":635},"dfEDd3Ew8CAUT4wW4aulZjujbPVrsMOFkCh11XYADpo",[643,645],{"title":96,"path":97,"stem":98,"description":644,"icon":99},"The rules installed with the app, what each one watches, and when it fires.",{"title":106,"path":107,"stem":108,"description":646,"icon":109},"Acknowledge, assign, merge, split and close incidents, and write the postmortem.",1795109740256]